section.para:
Each notifications/message frame carries a JSON-LD document in its params.message field. Every event document shall include:
@context — a URI pointing to the canonical LinkML schema for this event type. The ONVIF Client shall use this URI for schema lookup and for dynamic schema re-registration (see ).
@type — the event class name as defined in the registered schema (for example FireDetectionEvent). The ONVIF Client shall use this field for event routing.
All mandatory fields of the concrete Observation subclass identified by @type, as defined in the registered LinkML schema. For example, a SOSAObservation () requires sosa:madeBySensor, sosa:observedProperty, sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest, sosa:hasResult, sosa:phenomenonTime, and sosa:resultTime. Other Observation subclasses shall populate their own mandatory fields as declared in their respective schema class.

section.programlisting:
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 8,
  "result": {
    "resultType": "complete",
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "get_status",
        "description": "Returns the operational status of the AI engine.",
        "inputSchema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {},
          "required": []
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
